              ":question/id": "35290ca2-1488-52ba-9d2e-b8c3e04c45e4",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4743",
              ":question/problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{12}.$",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Note that $12=4 \\cdot 3,$ where $4$ is a perfect square. So, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{12} =\\sqrt{4 \\cdot 3}= \\sqrt{4} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 2\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "202575c6-7672-5387-a5ae-762bef520add",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Separating a Square Root Into a Product of Two Square Roots"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186124482,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186124295,
              ":question/id": "204328e4-810f-591e-a085-bb9cdadca875",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4744",
              ":question/problem": "Write $3 \\sqrt{5}$ as the square root of a single number.",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Note that $3 = \\sqrt{9}.$ So, applying the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sqrt{5} = \\sqrt{9}\\cdot\\sqrt{5}= \\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} = \\sqrt{45}.\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "d6f8c2c9-e82f-5d37-9f34-4811dd88c78d",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "Writing a Product of Two Square Roots as a Single Square Root"
          },
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186124483,
            ":knowledge-point/canonical-example": {
              ":db/id": 17592186124296,
              ":question/id": "0c797a57-00a8-57b9-af30-655e8952c4c3",
              ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4756",
              ":question/problem": "Express $\\sqrt[3]{2}\\cdot\\sqrt[3]{3}$ as the cube root of a single number.",
              ":question/worked-solution": "Using the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{2}\\cdot\\sqrt[3]{3}= \\sqrt[3]{2\\cdot 3} = \\sqrt[3]{6}.\n$$"
            },
            ":knowledge-point/id": "e97098b0-a7f9-564a-899e-60fb88682c80",
            ":knowledge-point/title": "The Product Rule With Cube Roots"
          }
